    "Scouting Notes": "Starter\n Fastball isn't great, but strong  4 VAA and command makes up for some iffy metrics outside of it.\n Cutter/slider offering in the 86 88 MPH range is a nice secondary that bridges the gap between the fastball and the curve well\n Curve is still a plus plus pitch, put away type pitch\n Changeup is lagging still, but made some strides, could wind up an average pitch\n Really strong command\n Still struggling to stay healthy, but good to see him back, he looks like a big league arm",
    "Notes Updated 2": "1/5/2024",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Starter\n Fastball isn't great, but strong  4 VAA and command makes up for some iffy metrics outside of it.\n Slider is plus\n Curve might be better\n Both could be plus, curve maybe even ++\n Changeup is lagging\n Really strong command\n Recovering from TJ, likely will miss most or all of next year, but I like the pickup a lot and think he could be a long term starter",
